 "note": "L5 RELAY KINDS. Three short lanes from A's relay column (RT, SW, RC, all A's) toward B. Top: the retract RT pulls in its short deck to T1 (B's line T1 -> RT falls). Middle: the switch SW trades its short deck to S1 (s1, up at the start) for the long diagonal to S2 (s2) - B's line S1 -> SW falls. Bottom: the remote console RC, whose lit conduit runs to the far deck pair at B's home: S1 - BH (m1, up at the start) swaps for M2 - BH (m2) - B's line BH -> S1 falls. Every relay deck is the short way for B's scripted line; fixed decks (RC - S2 - S1 - T1 - M2, S2 - BH) keep the board whole. Names: H, RT (retract), SW (switch), RC (remote console), T1, S1, S2, M2, BH.",
